<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade-Aug 4.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade-Aug 4.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Aug 1</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     360	   1.16     557250  200.61   16.80</p>
<p>State Bank	   320	   1.03     542600  173.63   16.78</p>
<p>Telco		  390	   1.24     255600   99.68   16.58</p>
<p>TISCO		  220	   0.65     347450   76.44   15.41</p>
<p>Castrol (BC)	 715	  20.41	94300   67.42   37.21</p>
<p>Reliance cap	  74	   0.24     680500   50.36   16.91</p>
<p>G.E.Shipping	  48	   0.15     969100   46.52   16.29</p>
<p>Colgate		330	  14.83     137300   45.31   58.58</p>
<p>Nestle		 285	   0.94     142400   40.58   17.20</p>
<p>Sterlite	     240	   0.77     165300   39.67   16.73</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 16.75 percent on an annualised basis against 18.75 percent in the previous carry forward account ended July 26.</p>
<p>Note :- BC - Book Closure</p>
